Anglo did not confirm the figure,

291
00:10:47,248 --> 00:10:48,970
and said it was not exclusive with

292
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:50,144
any buyer.

293
00:10:50,264 --> 00:10:51,889
But even as a rough guide,

294
00:10:51,889 --> 00:10:53,674
the gap is enormous.

295
00:10:53,674 --> 00:10:55,517
Almost thirteen billion dollars,

296
00:10:55,517 --> 00:10:56,244
then.

297
00:10:56,244 --> 00:10:57,898
Perhaps one billion,

298
00:10:57,898 --> 00:10:58,779
now.

299
00:10:59,017 --> 00:11:01,595
So what is the lesson of De

300
00:11:01,595 --> 00:11:02,517
Beers?

301
00:11:02,667 --> 00:11:04,605
That a price is not only about

302
00:11:04,605 --> 00:11:06,497
how rare something is.

303
00:11:06,527 --> 00:11:08,995
It is about who controls the supply,

304
00:11:08,995 --> 00:11:11,407
and what story people believe.

305
00:11:11,697 --> 00:11:14,517
De Beers mastered both for a century.

306
00:11:14,527 --> 00:11:16,066
It held the stones back,

307
00:11:16,066 --> 00:11:18,227
and it gave them a meaning.

308
00:11:18,367 --> 00:11:20,537
The slogan still works.

309
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:22,835
But a story can only hold a

310
00:11:22,835 --> 00:11:24,824
price up for as long as people

311
00:11:24,824 --> 00:11:26,813
stop asking what the thing would cost

312
00:11:26,813 --> 00:11:28,159
without it.

313
00:11:28,417 --> 00:11:30,908
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

314
00:11:30,908 --> 00:11:33,879
we follow the money behind another hidden

315
00:11:33,879 --> 00:11:36,307
link of the world economy.

316
00:11:36,527 --> 00:11:39,048
This is The Hidden Economics.
